  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNHCR activities in Turkey, 2014-2015</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNHCR is the main responsible for refugee efforts in the region. As the neighboring countries&apos; governments are increasingly introducing measures to limit the possibility to seek refuge or access public services in these countries, UNHCR has an increasingly important role in ensuring the protection of refugees and to assist countries in coping with the many refugees. This is also true in Turkey, where there in the recent months has been a particularly sharp rise in the number of refugees crossing the borders to the country from both Syria and Iraq. UNHCR estimates that 1,1 million Syrians are now located in Turkey. Meanwhile, only 29 per cent. of RRP&apos;en for Turkey is fulfilled. The Danish contribution is therefore a exceptionally earmarked for the efforts in Turkey in 2014.</narrative>
  </description>
